# The new MassOS upgrade utility (upgrade-massos) uses preupgrade_ng.
# This older file was only used by the now-unsupported older utility.
# As trying to perform an upgrade with it isn't supported, just crash.
# Upgrading from original MassOS (pre-2023) is not allowed.
cat > /dev/stderr << "END"
This legacy upgrade utility is no longer supported, and for safety, upgrades
are no longer permitted to be performed using it.

Please use the newer upgrade utility instead - see the following URL for info
about the new upgrade utility, as well as instructions on how to use it:

  https://github.com/MassOS-Linux/upgrade-massos

Please note that upgrades cannot be performed from experimental builds older
than experimental-20251105, nor can they be performed from any pre-2023 version
(e.g. 2022.10). If you are therefore using such a version, please back up your
data and perform a clean reinstallation of the latest version of MassOS. You
can refer to the official MassOS installation guide if you are unsure about how
to do this:

  https://github.com/MassOS-Linux/MassOS/wiki/Installing-MassOS

To check what MassOS version you are currently using, run the following command
in a terminal:

  massos-release

Thank you for using MassOS.
END
exit 1
